# flo-plugin conventions

This is a **public** npm package and GitHub repo. See `AGENTS.md` for full
context.

## Critical: public repo security

Never add to this repo:
- Secrets, tokens, API keys, or passwords
- Non-public infrastructure URLs (anything outside `*.floapp.co`)
- AWS account IDs or private ARNs
- Employee personal information

## MCP server (`src/index.js`)

- Single-file plain ESM — no build step, no TypeScript
- All tools declared in the `tools[]` array; all handlers in the `CallToolRequestSchema` handler
- Keep external dependencies to an absolute minimum (`npx` startup time is user-visible)
- New tool pattern: add to `tools[]` → add handler block → done

## npm publishing

- Publish via tag only: `git tag vX.Y.Z && git push origin vX.Y.Z`
- Never run `npm publish` manually (provenance attestation requires GitHub Actions)
- Bump `version` in `package.json` before tagging
- Tag format must be `vX.Y.Z` to trigger `.github/workflows/publish.yml`

## Commit messages

Follow Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:` only, ≤72 chars).

## Monorepo relationship

Changes here should eventually be synced back to
`Flomenco-Inc/flo:packages/flo-claude-plugin-mcp/`. That sync is manual
(no automation yet). Note the sync in your PR description.
